@startuml feature_flagging_service_workflow

title Feature Flagging Service Workflow (HTTP + WebSocket Broadcast)

actor Developer
actor "Backend Service / SDK" as Service
participant "Angular Dashboard" as Dashboard
participant "Presentation\nLayer" as PL
participant "Application\nLayer" as AL
participant "Domain\nLayer" as DL
participant "Infrastructure\nLayer" as IL
database "MySQL" as DB
collections "Ristretto\nL1 Cache" as L1
database "Redis\nL2 Cache" as CACHE
queue "Outbox\nDispatcher" as OUTBOX
queue "Message Broker" as MQ
participant "WebSocket\nBroadcaster" as WS
collections "Snapshot Files" as SNAP
participant "In-memory\nReconnect Events" as RECON
participant "Circuit\nBreaker" as CB

note over Dashboard, Service
    Dashboard/admin workflows use HTTP commands and query-side reads.
    Service-to-service consumers connect over WebSocket, receive all
    scoped flags, then wait for committed change broadcasts.
end note

== Service WebSocket Connect and Initial Flag State ==
Service -> WS: Connect /v1/broadcast/flags(projectId, environmentKey)
WS -> AL: Load authorized flag state for scope
AL -> L1: Get scoped flag read model

alt L1 Hit
L1 --> AL: Full scoped flag set
else L1 Miss
AL -> AL: Start per-scope singleflight refill
AL -> CACHE: Get scoped flag read model

alt L2 Hit
CACHE --> AL: Full scoped flag set
AL -> L1: Refill L1 with scoped flag set
else L2 Miss, Redis Failure, or Recovery
AL -> IL: Load flag definitions

alt DB Available
IL -> DB: Query flags, rules, segments
DB --> IL: Current committed definitions
AL -> CACHE: Refill L2 with scoped flag set
AL -> L1: Refill L1 with scoped flag set
IL --> AL: Full scoped flag set
else DB Failure
AL -> CB: Record DB failure for scope
IL -> SNAP: Load newest valid snapshot
SNAP --> IL: Snapshot flag definitions
note over AL, L1
    Degraded cache fill: entries populated from file fallback
    use a short TTL (e.g., 1 hour) and must be singleflight-guarded.
end note
AL -> L1: Refill L1 with snapshot data (short TTL)
alt Redis reachable (L2 available)
AL -> CACHE: Refill L2 with snapshot data (short TTL)
else Redis unreachable
AL -> AL: Skip L2 refill
end
IL --> AL: Full scoped flag set from snapshot
end
end
end

AL --> WS: Full scoped flag set
WS -> Service: WebSocket flags.snapshot(flags, scopeVersion)
Service -> Service: Replace/build local read state

note over WS, Service
    flag-gen is the WebSocket server.
    If a client disconnects, the client reconnects.
    On reconnect, flag-gen repeats this full scoped snapshot flow.
end note

== Redis Disconnect and Reconnect ==
AL -> CACHE: Read/write cache
CACHE --> AL: Connection error
AL -> RECON: Publish redis.disconnected event
RECON -> IL: Start reconnect if mutex is free

alt Reconnect mutex acquired
IL -> CACHE: Reconnect with backoff
CACHE --> IL: Reconnected
IL -> DB: Reload hot read models if needed
DB --> IL: Current committed definitions
IL -> CACHE: Refill cache
else Reconnect already running
RECON -> RECON: Drop/merge duplicate reconnect event
end

AL -> IL: Continue read without Redis

alt DB Available
IL -> DB: Try DB read
DB --> IL: Current committed definitions
else DB unavailable during Redis outage
IL -> SNAP: Load newest valid snapshot
SNAP --> IL: Snapshot flag definitions
end

== Flag Creation / Update with Transactional Outbox ==
Developer -> Dashboard: Create or update flag
Dashboard -> PL: POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/environments/{env}/flags
PL -> AL: CreateFlagCommand(actor, idempotencyKey)
AL -> DL: Flag.create()
DL -> DL: Validate key, value, rules, rollout
DL --> AL: FlagCreated event

AL -> IL: Begin unit of work
IL -> DB: BEGIN
IL -> DB: INSERT/UPDATE flag
IL -> DB: INSERT flag_version
IL -> DB: INSERT audit_entry
IL -> DB: INSERT outbox_event(eventId, aggregateVersion)
IL -> DB: COMMIT
IL --> AL: Committed flag state and outbox event
AL --> PL: Command result with version and outboxEventId
PL --> Dashboard: 201 Created / 200 OK
AL -> SNAP: Refresh snapshot from committed state

note over DB, OUTBOX
    DB commit is the consistency boundary.
    Message publish is async and retryable.
    Snapshot files are advanced only after
    the mutation flow succeeds.
end note

== Outbox Dispatch and Broadcast ==
OUTBOX -> DB: Poll pending outbox events
DB --> OUTBOX: FlagCreated/FlagUpdated event
OUTBOX -> MQ: Publish flag change event

alt Publish Success
MQ --> OUTBOX: Ack
OUTBOX -> DB: Mark event as published
MQ -> WS: Deliver flag change event
WS -> Service: WebSocket flag.updated/deleted(eventId, flag payload, scopeVersion, version)
Service -> Service: Deduplicate event and upsert/delete local read state
else Publish Failure
MQ --> OUTBOX: Publish failed
OUTBOX -> DB: Increment retry count; keep pending
OUTBOX -> OUTBOX: Retry with backoff
end

== HTTP Bootstrap / Recovery Evaluation ==
Service -> PL: POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/environments/{env}/flags/evaluate
PL -> AL: EvaluateFlagsQuery(context, flagKeys)
AL -> L1: Get scoped flag read model

alt L1 Hit
L1 --> AL: Flag definitions
else L1 Miss
AL -> AL: Start per-scope singleflight refill
AL -> CACHE: Get scoped flag read model

alt L2 Hit
CACHE --> AL: Flag definitions
AL -> L1: Refill L1
else L2 Miss or Redis Failure
AL -> IL: Load flag definitions

alt DB Available
IL -> DB: Query flags, rules, segments
DB --> IL: Current committed definitions
IL -> SNAP: Create snapshot if missing
AL -> CACHE: Refill L2
AL -> L1: Refill L1
IL --> AL: Flag definitions from database
else Flag Not Found
IL -> DB: Query flag by key
DB --> IL: No matching flag
AL -> L1: Store not-found marker TTL=5m
IL --> AL: Flag not found
else DB Failure
AL -> CB: Record DB failure for scope
IL -> SNAP: Load newest valid snapshot

alt Snapshot Valid
SNAP --> IL: Snapshot data with version/checksum
note over AL, L1
    Degraded cache fill: entries populated from file fallback
    use a short TTL (e.g., 1 hour) and must be singleflight-guarded.
end note
AL -> L1: Refill L1 with snapshot data (short TTL)
alt Redis reachable (L2 available)
AL -> CACHE: Refill L2 with snapshot data (short TTL)
else Redis unreachable
AL -> AL: Skip L2 refill
end
IL --> AL: Flag definitions from snapshot
else Snapshot Missing or Corrupted
SNAP --> IL: Invalid snapshot
AL -> CB: Open circuit breaker
IL --> AL: No readable fallback available
AL --> PL: 503 service_degraded
end
end

end
end

note over AL, PL
    For HTTP remote reads, if L1/L2 miss, DB is unavailable,
    and no valid snapshot exists, the flow ends with 503 and
    opens the circuit breaker. It must not silently return a
    successful default evaluation unless the endpoint explicitly
    supports degraded defaults.
end note

AL -> DL: Flag.evaluate(EvaluationContext)
DL -> DL: Apply enabled state, rules, and stable rollout
DL --> AL: EvaluationResult(value, reason, source, version)
AL --> PL: Evaluation response
PL --> Service: 200 OK
Service -> Service: Execute feature logic

== HTTP Flag Not Found Negative Cache ==
Service -> PL: GET /v1/.../flags/missing_flag/evaluate
PL -> AL: EvaluateFlagQuery(flagKey)
AL -> L1: Check flag and not-found marker

alt L1 Not-found Marker Hit
L1 --> AL: not-found marker
AL --> PL: 404 flag_not_found
else Marker Miss
AL -> CACHE: Check L2/DB through normal read path
AL -> L1: Store not-found marker TTL=5m if DB confirms missing
AL --> PL: 404 flag_not_found
end

== Read Failure Circuit Breaker ==
Service -> PL: GET /v1/.../flags/evaluate
PL -> AL: EvaluateFlagsQuery
AL -> L1: Cache miss
AL -> CACHE: Cache miss or unavailable
AL -> CB: Check breaker state

alt Circuit Open
CB --> AL: open
AL --> PL: 503 circuit_open or valid fallback response
else Circuit Closed or Half-open
AL -> DB: Try DB read
DB --> AL: Connection failure
AL -> SNAP: Try newest valid snapshot
SNAP --> AL: Missing or corrupted
AL -> CB: Open breaker with backoff
AL --> PL: 503 service_degraded
end

== Runtime Evaluation from Local State ==
Service -> Service: Evaluate flag from local read state/cache
Service -> Service: Apply enabled state, rules, and stable rollout
Service -> Service: Execute feature logic without DB dependency

== Concurrent Update Handling ==
Developer -> Dashboard: Update flag using version=1
Dashboard -> PL: PATCH /v1/projects/{projectId}/environments/{env}/flags/{flagId}
PL -> AL: UpdateFlagCommand(version=1)
AL -> DL: Flag.update()
DL -> DL: Check current version

alt Version Matches
DL --> AL: Valid update
AL -> IL: Commit flag + version + audit + outbox event
IL -> DB: UPDATE flag SET version=2 WHERE version=1
DB --> IL: Updated
AL --> PL: 200 OK
PL --> Dashboard: Update successful
else Version Conflict
DL --> AL: Version mismatch
AL -> AL: Log conflict with correlation ID
AL --> PL: 409 Conflict
PL --> Dashboard: Version outdated
end

== Snapshot Corruption During Failover ==
Service -> PL: POST /v1/projects/{projectId}/environments/{env}/flags/evaluate while DB unavailable
PL -> AL: EvaluateFlagsQuery
AL -> IL: Load fallback snapshot
IL -> SNAP: Read snapshot
SNAP --> IL: Checksum mismatch
IL -> IL: Log corruption and mark snapshot invalid
IL --> AL: Safe defaults
AL -> DL: Evaluate using safe defaults
DL --> AL: EvaluationResult(source="default")
AL --> PL: Degraded evaluation result
PL --> Service: 200 OK with fallback metadata

note over DL
    Domain layer owns flag invariants, rule matching,
    stable rollout, and evaluation result reasons.
end note

note over IL, DB
    Infrastructure persists aggregate state, versions,
    audit entries, outbox records, cache entries, and snapshots.
end note

note over OUTBOX, WS
    Outbox plus idempotent consumers avoids rollback of
    already-published messages and minimizes update errors.
end note

@enduml
